"Alan is a man from Provo, Utah, on Earth."
"Alan reads a lot of books, these days mostly LitRPG, and watches anime."
"Alan is autistic and has total aphantasia."
"Alan speed reads some four thousand words a minute, with its grasp whole."
"The last thing Alan remembers is going to sleep in his own bed at home in Provo."
"Everything after that is fog to her, and she cannot say how she came to be where she woke."
"Alan woke in a woman's body."
"In this body she calls herself Nala."
"Her body looks about twenty-five, slim, and a head shorter than Alan was."
"Her skin is pale and fair, with a dusting of freckles across her nose and cheeks."
"Her eyes are blue-grey."
"Her hair is dark auburn-red, straight and heavy, long enough to pool in her lap when she sits."
"Her hands are small and narrow and pale, freckled on the back."
"Her voice is a woman's, low for a woman and a little rough."
"She wears Alan's loose grey sleep shirt, which hangs off her and slips off one shoulder."
"She wears Alan's black shorts, too big to stay up on her hips."
"She wears Alan's black compression tights, which still fit her snugly and stay up."
"She has no shoes, no coat, no phone, no money, no keys and no papers."
"No one in this world knows her."
"Nala came to on the Belmont platform at 4:40 on the morning of Saturday, January 31st."
"Nala has no power, and the System has never chosen her."
"No record of her exists in this world: no birth, no name, no prints, no face on file."
"Nala crossed along the link a wordchain makes between a chainer and an Opposite on another world."
"That night a lonely girl in Chicago chained with the words wrong, asking for a sister, not luck."
"Alan was the Opposite the chain reached, and the whole of him crossed rather than a portion."
"Her body was made new in the crossing, shaped to the sister the chain asked for."
"The body is wholly hers now, healthy and whole, and ages like any human's."
"The chain set her down near the girl who spoke it, on the Belmont platform."
"The girl who chained does not know her chain was answered."
"The System holds no record of the crossing and knows nothing of Nala."
